        "original_id": "9fd95bb4-1f9b-5693-9aec-15ff48e987e1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: Cascade Locks and Canal, Oregon Portage Railroad\n- Places: Columbia River, Oregon, Washington, Palm Beach County, Florida, Lake Worth Lagoon, Tanner Creek, Bonneville Dam\n\nFacts:\n- The Cascade Locks and Canal was a navigation project on the Columbia River between the U.S. states of Oregon and Washington.\n- The Cascade Locks and Canal was completed in 1896.\n- The Oregon Portage Railroad ran from Tanner Creek to the Cascade Locks during the later years of its operation.\n- Tanner Creek was near the site where Bonneville Dam was later built.\n- The Cascade Locks were under construction during the later years of the Oregon Portage Railroad's operation.\n- Lake Worth Lagoon is a lagoon located in Palm Beach County, Florida.",
